{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Apart from the burnt-offering of the daily sacrifice.</b> And if you ask: why is it not written 'apart from the two loaves and the seven lambs and the bull and the two rams and the goat and the seven lambs that come with them,' just as it is written 'apart from the burnt-offering of the new month and its meal-offering etc.' and 'apart from the sin-offering of atonements and the burnt-offering of the daily sacrifice'? One may answer: since it is written 'when you offer a new meal-offering,' it has already been mentioned, and they come upon the meal-offering, and nothing more is needed." "<b>And their libations.</b> This refers to the wine libations of the day of first fruits, and to the wine libations and the meal-offering libations of the daily burnt-offering."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:08.040336387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}